e democratic  convention a kind of a feeling the  wheels are falling off the cart  in 1980 you have stagflation  you have a feeling that the energy  crisis is out of control people are in  gas lines  iranian students take uh hostages at the  american embassy in tehran  again a feeling the wheels are coming  off the cart so how does it work this  time  you would think it's not good news for  the incumbent but it's also been good  news for the law and order candidate in  the past  in late june trump attempted to take his  campaign back on the road to tulsa  the campaign schedules a rally in tulsa  oklahoma  they're looking for a location with low  cases of virus they think they can do it  safely  and they schedule it for juneteenth  which is of course the celebration of  emancipation of slaves in america  and activists there were concerned that  him being there amid all this unrest  and in tulsa specifically which has such  a  dark history tulsa was the site of one  of the worst race riots in u.s history  after critics accused the president of  insensitivity the rally was rescheduled  for june 20th  but on the day of the event things  didn't go as planned  the campaign started estimating that  hundreds of thousands of people were  going to descend upon tulsa for this  rally  in reality only about 6 000 people show  up and it's the first rally  in five years that is half empty for  trump until this point both candidates  had relied on virtual events to get  their message out  joe biden is really a retail politician  he  loves to be in front of people and he  loves to get close to them and have  personal conversations and give hugs and  this campaign has not played to those  strengths  for a lot of the summer joe biden was  not terribly visible  the the trump joke was that he was  hiding in his basement  but really he was doing interviews and  tv appearances  and zoom appearances the reason i'm so  optimistic is because of your generation  600 000 brave postal workers deserve our  full support  the biden campaign's argument was number  one we're listening to the scientists  and they say it's not safe to do these  things  and number two they felt like they just  needed to stay out of trump's way  and let him make his own mess on august  11th  bine announced kamala harris as his  running mate your next vice president  united states kamala harris this  fulfilled a promise  he made back in march i commit that i  will in fact appoint a  i'll pick a woman to be vice president  there was a lot of  pressure on joe biden to pick a black  woman  because of the widespread support he had  gained from  black people during the primary and  saying that black people had saved his  campaign  she was the obvious choice a woman of  color who had  done respectably well as a candidate  herself and who had  a significant base in california a lot  of money  support the obvious and in some ways the  safest  choice after being postponed for a month  because of coronavirus concerns  the dnc kicked off in august but the  four-day event was significantly  downsized  most of the speakers participated  virtually or pre-taped their comments  even the candidate didn't travel to the  host city milwaukee  to accept his nomination usually there  are thousands and thousands of people  packed into a stadium or an arena for a  few days  we basically saw none of that this year  the message that democrats and joe biden  were trying to get across  was that joe biden is portraying him as  a healer  showing that he's someone who has been  through grief and tragedy and can bring  people together  at the convention the democrats  definitely want to put the focus on the  pandemic and  the recession they really try to draw a  connection between  the president's handling of the virus  and  how that relates to not only the economy  but also on how it affects their  livelihood and trying to speak to the  frustrations people feel with the  lockdowns we'll have a national mandate  